{
  "book": "DAN",
  "chapter": 3,
  "resources": {
    "costumbres": {
      "c-4991feca4a8517a3": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-593",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "It is not easy to tell the precise articles of costume intended by the original words which our translators have rendered as above, though the improved sources or exposition in our day add to the knowledge which they possessed. Bevan, in Smith's Dictionary of the Bible, vol.1, p.…",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-593",
          "sourceHash": "ae0710642c66fbab0c6831e7cad28e148c2ff8ffedb865a94174e3c20bd2d970",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      },
      "c-4dd7696c0eb684b7": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-590",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "See verses 7, 10, and 15. The monuments amply testify to the fondness of the Babylonians for music. They had numerous instruments, and organized large hands. Annarus, a Babylonian noble, entertained his guests at a banquet with music, vocal and instrumental, performed by a band o…",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-590",
          "sourceHash": "d4ad944b31c6988306c40c96409c175ca3d1966c4f75ee42df7618790f6d781e",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      },
      "c-c584d006165066ac": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-592",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "On the monuments discovered at Khorsabad there are representations of gigantic and muscular men, like the “mighty men” of the text, who seem to have been always in attendance on the king, waiting to execute his orders. Such men were selected from the army on account of their size…",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-592",
          "sourceHash": "63b5125668e23d6dcf93ceac26137e711fdbf0f82106a62dac52befc8edad659",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      },
      "c-c60da79b9b57f630": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-591",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "And whoso falleth not down and worshipeth shall the same hour be cast into the midst of a burning fiery furnace.",
        "traduccion": {
          "resourceId": "freeman-591",
          "sourceHash": "de610da19d821873e569963241494cac8a76ff7e00ad5991efea75785313740c",
          "sourceLanguage": "en"
        }
      }
    },
